help build our intuition of this data structure let's make a simple plotting function to visualise haplotypes."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"metadata":{"tags":[],"id":"IQDFHy06gzYW","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1749083975288,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":53,"user":{"displayName":"Moureen Caroline","userId":"15363393983719029940"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["def plot_haplotypes(\n","    ds,\n","    hide_text=False,\n","    hide_non_seg=False,\n","):\n","    import plotly.express as px\n","    import allel\n","\n","    # convert to 2D array of haplotypes\n","    pos = ds[\"variant_position\"].values\n","    gt = ds[\"call_genotype\"].values\n","    ht = gt.reshape(gt.shape[0], -1)\n","\n","    # size rows and columns\n","    if hide_text:\n","        # can make smaller because text not shown\n","        row_height = 8\n","        col_width = 5\n","    else:\n","        # make a bit bigger so we can see the text\n","        row_height = 14\n","        col_width = 12\n","\n","    # deal with non-segregating sites\n","    if hide_non_seg:\n","        ac = allel.HaplotypeArray(ht).count_alleles(max_allele=1)\n","        loc_seg = ac.is_segregating()\n","        ht = ht[loc_seg]\n","\n","    # plot a heatmap\n","    fig = px.imshow(\n","        ht.T,\n","        text_auto=not hide_text,\n","        labels=dict(\n","            x=\"Variants\",\n","            y=\"Haplotypes\",\n","        ),\n","        width=ht.shape[0] * col_width + 200,\n","        height=ht.shape[1] * row_height + 200,\n","        zmin=0,\n","        zmax=0,\n","        color_continuous_scale=\"greys\",\n","        template=\"simple_white\",\n","        aspect=\"auto\"\n","    )\n","\n","    # visual styling\n","    fig.update_layout(\n","        coloraxis_showscale=False,\n","        plot_bgcolor=\"#cccccc\",\n","    )\n","    fig.update_traces(xgap=0, ygap=1)\n","    fig.update_xaxes(tickvals=[])\n","    fig.update_yaxes(tickvals=[])\n","\n","    return fig"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"zCQtxDkEgzYX"},"source":["This function will visualise haplotypes as a heatmap, with haplotypes as rows and variants as columns. A reference allele has a white background, and an alternate allele has a black background.\n","\n","Let's use the function to visualise the haplotypes we accessed above."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"metadata":{"tags":[],"id":"884zawGTgzYX","outputId":"afaca460-7d53-46a6-c8a7-a1b381c85f50","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":777,"output_embedded_package_id":"1vWM-89Wh-8NWWo4ZH88s4v2l5BCTPa64"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1749083994422,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":5470,"user":{"displayName":"Moureen Caroline","userId":"15363393983719029940"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Output hidden; open in https://colab.research.google.com to view."},"metadata":{}}],"source":["plot_haplotypes(ds_haps)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"zmHPcwfTgzYc"},"source":["In this set of haplotype data we can see there are only two variants which are segregating in this set of samples. All the other variants are non-segregating, which means all haplotypes carry the same allele (in this case a \"0\" meaning the reference allele).\n","\n","The non-segregating variants are not particularly informative, so let's hide them."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"metadata":{"tags":[],"id":"Cpm1h0BUgzYc","outputId":"54753fc9-9bca-452c-d92b-03dc658df9b6","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":777},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1749084006362,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":968,"user":{"displayName":"Moureen Caroline","userId":"15363393983719029940"}}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/html":["<html>\n","<head><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /></head>\n","<body>\n","    <div>            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.5/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS-MML_SVG\"></script><script type=\"text/javascript